  "sticker": "hedgehog",
  "skeleton": "hedgehog standing, three-quarter view facing left: root on the ground; body (the spiny back) with belly squash; head (the cream face and snout) at the front-left, face with eyes and mouth; four little feet under the body; a curled-up ball piece swaps in for everything when it curls.",
  "sheets": [
    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a hedgehog character. Draw this exact hedgehog as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate body parts laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every part at the size it has in image 1.\n\nDraw each part on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no part touching or overlapping another:\n1. the body: the round body covered in brown spines with its cream tummy below, drawn whole including the part behind the head, without head or feet.\n2. the head: the cream face and snout with its black nose and small round ear, facing left as in image 1, with a completely blank face — no eyes, no mouth — keep the nose, the cheek and the ear; without spines; its back edge rounded.\n3. one foot: a small cream foot with a short leg.\n4. the hedgehog curled up into a round ball of brown spines, no face showing.\n\nEvery part is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another part, and each joint end (where it tucks under the body or the head) is a full, smooth, rounded edge. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the parts beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows. Fully transparent background."
    },
    {
      "id": "face",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "references": [
        "parts"
      ],
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a hedgehog character; image 2 shows the same hedgehog cut into puppet parts, with a blank face. Draw the hedgehog's face pieces as separate stickers on one sheet: the same drawing style, colours and line as in image 1, every piece at the size it has on the hedgehog in image 1, so it fits the blank face in image 2.\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out in tidy rows with wide empty gaps between them, nothing touching:\n1. the hedgehog's left eye (on the right of image 1) as it is in image 1: a dark round eye with a white sparkle and a slightly worried brow.\n2. the same eye wide open and surprised: bigger and rounder, with its white sparkle.\n3. the same eye gently closed in sleep: a soft downward-curving line with a few lashes.\n4. the same eye closed in a happy smile: an upward-curving arc.\n5. the same eye sad: looking down, its upper lid tilted up towards the middle.\n6. the mouth as it is in image 1: a small smile.\n7. the mouth wide open in a big happy laugh, the inside pink.\n8. the mouth open in a small round 'o'.\n9. the mouth in a small sad frown.\n\nNo text, no labels, no numbers, no shadows, no face or head around the pieces. Fully transparent background."
    }
